Draw terminal box-drawing characters to full cell boundaries.

cosmic-term renders terminal rows as shaped text. That leaves box-drawing
characters at the mercy of the selected font's glyph bounds; with a normal
terminal line height, vertical border glyphs such as U+2502 can leave small gaps
between rows. Draw the common box-drawing set as simple terminal primitives over
the font glyphs so panes and zellij frames connect at cell edges.

--- a/src/terminal_box.rs
+++ b/src/terminal_box.rs
@@ -719,6 +719,22 @@
             position: view_position,
             color: Color::from_rgba(1.0, 1.0, 1.0, 1.0), // TODO
             clip_bounds: Rectangle::new(view_position, Size::new(view_w as f32, view_h as f32)),
+        });
+
+        // Font glyphs for box-drawing characters often do not fill the terminal
+        // line height, leaving visible gaps between adjacent rows. Overlay the
+        // common box-drawing characters as cell-aligned primitives so terminal
+        // frames connect exactly.
+        terminal.with_buffer(|buffer| {
+            for run in buffer.layout_runs() {
+                draw_box_drawing_run(
+                    renderer,
+                    &terminal,
